AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#inSubset> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_00000081> "envoPolar")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_00000081> "A mountain is generally steeper than a hill, but there is no universally accepted standard definition for the height of a mountain or a hill although a mountain usually has an identifiable summit. The USGS had previously defined mountains as localised elevations of more than 300 meters; however, the organisation has accepted there are no technical definitions in the US. In ENVO, we primarily use the UNEP-WCMC classification to be compliant with SDG monitoring, but we can host other classifications on request: http://www.fao.org/sustainable-development-goals/indicators/1542/en/")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_00000081> "mountain")
