# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000122> (marine hydrothermal vent)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ISBN:978-0-444-82619-0") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ORCID:0000-0002-4366-3088") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000122> "A marine hydrothermal vent is a marine benthic feature where heat generated due to tectonic activity, either at divergent plate boundaries or convergent ocean plates where back-arc spreading occurs, is released or 'vented' to the surface. The resultant high temperature water jets are laden with dissolved metals and minerals.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#created_by> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000122> "ORCID:0000-0002-4366-3088")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#creation_date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000122> "2010-03-17T02:13:33Z")
