# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000140> (whale fall)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whale_fall") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000140> "Whale fall is the term used for a whale carcass that has fallen to the ocean floor. When a whale dies in shallow water, its carcass is typically devoured by scavengers over a relatively short period of time: within several months. However, in deeper water (depths of 2,000 m/6,600 ft or greater), fewer scavenger species exist, and the carcass can provide sustenance for a complex localized ecosystem over periods of decades.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#created_by> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000140> "ORCID:0000-0002-4366-3088")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#creation_date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000140> "2010-03-20T06:26:13Z")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasOBONamespace> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000140> "ENVO")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#id> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000140> "ENVO:01000140")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000140> "whale fall")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000140> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01000139>)

