# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001517> (drift ice mass)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4808-4736>) <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001517> "A floating mass of ice which is 1) unattached to land or land-fast ice and 2) moved by the action of winds or currents.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#created_by> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001517> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4366-3088>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#creation_date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001517> "2019-01-14T19:46:20Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasBroadSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001517> "drift ice")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001517> "http://sweetontology.net/realmCryo/DriftIce")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001517> "Prior to approximately 2014, drift ice was synonymous with the various grades of pack ice, described as very open (with an ice concentration of 1/10 to 3/10), open (4/10 to 6/10, with many leads and polynyas and the floes generally not in contact with one another), close (7/10 to 8/10, composed of floes mostly in contact), very close (9/10 to less than 10/10), and compact (10/10, with no water visible, called consolidated pack ice if the floes are frozen together). This is deprecated, with pack ice now referring to drift ice with a concentration equal to or above 7/10; however, other usages are still common.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001517> "drift ice mass"@en)
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001517> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ENVO_01001345>)

